  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1974-p14.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "If \\(x\\lt0,\\) then \\(x^2\\gt0\\gt x,\\) so choice A always holds. The values \\(x=-1,\\) \\(x=-1,\\) \\(x=2,\\) and \\(x=-1\\) respectively disprove B, C, D, and E.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "For a negative \\(x,\\) compare \\(x^2\\) first with zero",
        "Simple test values such as \\(-1,\\) \\(\\frac12,\\) and \\(2\\) reject the other implications"
      ],
